  "body": "Fixes the red batch gate on main: `a_step_lathe_holder_placed_off_its_model_frame_is_judged_and_its_mirror_stands_clear` posted a turning setup through the default milling post, which the #1232 refusal now rejects by name (\"post Fanuc does not serve ... a turning machine\").\n\nWhat changed: the test (`crates/app/tests/vendor_tool_body.rs`) sets the document post to \"Fanuc Lathe\" (`posting::post_set`) before regenerating. The refusal is untouched and right: the test's setup was wrong.\n\nWhich merge made main red: two PRs that were each green alone. Refusal: 3f221475 (`fix(post): refuse by name a post that does not serve its setup's machine kind`), merged via cf27cd57 (PR for #1232). Test: 1a6d4017 (#361 vendor tool models), merged via 11baed7b. Neither saw the other; whichever landed second turned main red.\n\nOther tests: one grep of tests that load a lathe machine and post (drilling_axial, turning_blade, turning_holder, turning_insert_zone) found no other failing case in the red gate; only this test was reported.\n\nTested: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test vendor_tool_body` 3/3 pass; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. Not run: other suites.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium (issue labelled effort:low)\n\nFixes #1333\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
